{:edb/db-before-t 1526 :edb/db-after-t 1527 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534839 50 #inst "2026-10-12T21:55:55.631Z" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117248 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117249 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117250 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117251 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117252 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440571 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440581 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440589 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440608 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186117247 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440612 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186117247 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440581 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186119450 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186119451 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186119452 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186119453 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186119454 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440569 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440572 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440575 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440595 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440614 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119449 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440569 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119980 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440631 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119980 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440633 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119981 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440627 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119981 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440628 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119981 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440630 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119982 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440629 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119982 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440632 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119982 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440634 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186119983 1050 660.0 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186120181 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186120181 1071 "Find $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}c \\cdot f(t)dt$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}f(t)dt = 16i + 8j + 2k$\nand\n$c =-i + j$." 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186120181 1071 "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=16\\,i+8\\,j+2\\,k$ \nand \n$c=-i+j.$" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186120181 1074 "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-i+j)\\times (16\\,i+8\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 16 & 8\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(-2-0)j+(-8-16)k \\\\  & =2i+2j-24k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186120556 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186120556 1071 "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1}f(t) + ⟨1, 1, 1⟩dt$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{0}f(t)dt = ⟨ - 2, 3, 4⟩$." 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186120556 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)+⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩.$" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186120556 1074 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-3,\\,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)+⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-3,\\,-4⟩+{⟨t,\\,t,\\,t⟩|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-3,\\,-4⟩+⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186120557 1068 #edb/ref 17592186119455 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186120995 1064 "Since the integration of vector functions is done component-by-component, the properties of integrals of vector functions are immediately inherited from those of the integrals of real-valued functions. \n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are vector-valued functions that are continuous on a closed interval $[a,b],$ and $\\alpha$ is a scalar. \nThen, the *vector addition and scalar multiplication rules* are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}(f(t)+g(t))\\text{d}t={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\,+\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\, & \\text{vector addition rule} \\\\ {\\int }_{a}^{b}\\alpha \\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\alpha \\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\, & \\text{scalar constant multiple rule}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFor example, if $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle t, \\: \\cos t\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf g(t) = \\left\\langle -t^2, \\: \\sin t \\right\\rangle,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int [f(t)+2g(t)]\\text{d}t & =\\int f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2\\int g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}t⟩\\,\\text{d}t+2\\int ⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}t⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int t\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}t\\,\\text{d}t⟩+⟨2\\int -{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,2\\int \\operatorname{sin}t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+{C}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}t+{C}_{2}⟩+⟨-\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}+{C}_{3},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}t+{C}_{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3{t}^{2}-4{t}^{3}}{6},\\,\\operatorname{sin}t-2\\operatorname{cos}t⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C_1, \\, C_2, \\, C_3, \\, C_4$ are arbitrary real constants and ${\\mathbf C} = \\langle C_1+C_3, C_2+C_4 \\rangle$ is a constant vector." 13194139534839 17592186045417 false] [17592186120995 1064 "Since the integration of vector functions is done component-by-component, the properties of integrals of vector functions are immediately inherited from those of the integrals of real-valued functions. \n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are vector-valued functions that are continuous on a closed interval $[a,b],$ and $\\alpha$ is a scalar. \nThen, the *vector addition and scalar multiplication rules* are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}(f(t)+g(t))\\text{d}t={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\,+\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\, & \\text{vector addition rule} \\\\ {\\int }_{a}^{b}\\alpha \\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\alpha \\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\, & \\text{scalar constant multiple rule}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFor example, if $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle t, \\: \\cos t\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf g(t) = \\left\\langle -t^2, \\: \\sin t \\right\\rangle,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int [f(t)+2g(t)]\\text{d}t & =\\int f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2\\int g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t+2\\int ⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int t\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩+⟨2\\int -{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,2\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+{C}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{C}_{2}⟩+⟨-\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}+{C}_{3},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{C}_{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3{t}^{2}-4{t}^{3}}{6},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $C_1, \\, C_2, \\, C_3, \\, C_4$ are arbitrary real constants and ${\\mathbf C} = \\langle C_1+C_3, C_2+C_4 \\rangle$ is a constant vector." 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440569 1080 "⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-3⟩" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440569 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440569 1083 #uuid "00e985bc-3646-55e6-b3a2-05849e559813" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440570 1080 "10\\,i+17\\,j-12\\,k" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440570 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440570 1083 #uuid "0735890c-3c78-543f-89dd-6ca5377bb2e9" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440571 1080 "-2i+2j+24k" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440571 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440571 1083 #uuid "0c143a77-e1af-52aa-b7eb-98785edc55ae" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440572 1080 "⟨3,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440572 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440572 1083 #uuid "0c92cdac-b992-5f56-8073-a74a63b8e267" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440573 1080 "2\\,i+7\\,j-k" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440573 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440573 1083 #uuid "0d99e8a1-d9f3-5f82-af54-6968a95a1bf3" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440574 1080 "⟨-3,\\,7,\\,-3⟩" 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440574 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534839 17592186045417 true] [17592186440574 1083 #uuid "13aaa8